      "topLeftX": 124,
      "topLeftY": 466,
      "bottomRightX": 697,
      "bottomRightY": 584,
      "content": "The recommended mated connector impedance is needed to maintain signal integrity. The differential impedance of a mated connector should be 90 Ω +/-10 Ω, as seen from a 40 ps (20%-80%) risetime of a differential TDR. The impedance profile of a mated connector should fall within the limits shown in Figure 5-21. The impedance profile of the mated connector is defined from the receptacle footprints through the plug cable termination area. In a case where the plug is directly attached to a device PCB, the mated connector impedance profile includes the path from the receptacle footprints to the plug footprints.",
